WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.680
The Game of Thrones stars are finally able
to speak out about how this blockbuster fantasy

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.800
series came to a close, and while some are
happy with their endings, others, particularly

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.400
the Mother of Dragons, seem to be less than
thrilled.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.060
Throughout her run on Thrones, Emilia Clarke
has taken Daenerys Targaryen from a naïve,

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.529
frightened child bride to a formidable and
lethal dragon queen, but underneath it all,

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:23.840
Daenerys has had to juggle her desire for
justice with her genetic makeup.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.560
After all, she is the daughter of the infamous
Mad King, Aerys II Targaryen.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.239
Even so, audiences have always rooted for
Daenerys, cheering her on as she frees slaves,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.260
saves innocents, and fights those in power
to give it to those below, until the end of

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.260
season eight.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.380
Daenerys' torching of King's Landing during
the penultimate episode, "The Bells," wasn't

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.060
entirely unexpected, but her descent into
madness was seen as abrupt and unearned, as

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.190
if viewers were supposed to forget about Daenerys'
humanity and believe she would kill thousands

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.300
of innocent people without a passing thought.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.420
For her part, Clarke might have tried to warn
audiences about this before the season aired.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.580
In 2018, Clarke revealed to Vanity Fair that
her final scenes were incredibly upsetting

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:04.960
and that fans might look at Daenerys differently,
given that her continued passion for war leads

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.060
to Jon Snow ultimately having to kill her.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.620
During an Emmys event before the final season
premiered, it's hard to overlook her facial

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.620
expression:

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.900
"Best season ever!"

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.920
Other actors have expressed some frustrations
about the final season, too.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:18.920
They include...

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.460
One of the most compelling, infuriating, evil,
and dynamic characters on Game of Thrones

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.280
is Cersei Lannister, thanks in no small part
to the performance of Lena Headey.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.800
Even as Cersei committed unspeakable atrocities,
killing anyone and destroying everything in

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.140
her path to make sure the Lannisters stayed
in power, fans were occasionally swayed thanks

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.660
to the heart and depth Headey put into Cersei's
character.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:42.840
Fans expected an ending for Cersei that was
as sensational as Headey's performance.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.160
Unfortunately, Cersei's grand exit didn't
pan out as planned.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.820
While fans were mulling over theories that
ranged from everything from death by Jaime's

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:54.380
golden hand to Arya or the Hound killing Cersei,
they were ultimately given a sequence in which

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.820
Cersei and twin brother Jaime are crushed
by bricks in each others' arms in the bottom

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.000
of the Red Keep.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.200
Even Headey was annoyed at this closing scene,
saying she wanted something bigger or any

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.380
sort of fight at all.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.840
As freed slave Missandei, Nathalie Emmanuel
brought a considerable amount of heart to

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.100
an often cruel show.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.360
Fans loved her friendship with Daenerys as
well as her relationship with Grey Worm, the

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:18.550
leader of the Unsullied army, but grew apprehensive
when Missandei and Grey Worm started to make

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.060
plans for the future, always a bad sign.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.680
Missandei ended up captured by Cersei's forces,
and was beheaded in front of Daenerys in a

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.360
show of cruelty and power.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.170
After the episode, Emmanuel said that it was
disappointing to see the show's one woman

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.940
of color killed so abruptly.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.920
She also spoke to the emotional weight of
Missandei dying in chains, which brought her

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.400
full circle in the most heartbreaking way
possible.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.400
Fans and critics agreed with Emmanuel, and
it seems there's no shortage of viewers who

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.800
think there should have been more justice
for the character.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.960
One of the most mysterious and interesting
characters in Thrones, Lord Varys, played

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:53.380
by Conleth Hill, seemed to know every secret
in all of Westeros.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:57.560
Though Varys began the series firmly in the
Lannister camp, he eventually switched sides

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:00.020
to join his friend Tyrion Lannister in Daenerys'
court.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:03.420
Having known Daenerys' dangerous father, he
remained cautious.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.540
After Missandei's execution, he concocted
a plan to tell the Seven Kingdoms about the

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.380
true heir to the throne, Jon Snow, only to
be found out and burned alive at Daenerys'

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.380
order.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.960
After Varys' death, Hill told Entertainment
Weekly that he was upset by the last couple

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:16.960
of seasons.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.340
He was disappointed that the showrunners couldn't
devise a final meeting between Varys and Littlefinger,

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:25.340
considering that the two characters often
worked together to pull the strings.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.540
He added that he wasn't sure the series successfully
moved past author George R.R. Martin's source

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.540
material.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:35.380
"Are you all happy...with the outcome of the
show?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:36.940
Personally?"

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.120
By season eight, Tyrion Lannister had been
Daenerys' top advisor for quite some time,

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.940
but in her eyes, he'd begun to falter.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.180
Between underestimating his sinister sister
Cersei and being too trusting of his brother

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.800
Jaime, relations between the Dragon Queen
and her Hand were splintering.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.960
Actor Peter Dinklage certainly has a good
relationship with his character, but has also

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.280
made not-so-subtle hints at his frustration
with how the show ended.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:04.700
In a video about the end of the show, he criticized
the decision to put all the women and children

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.640
in a crypt full of the dead during the Battle
of Winterfell, but the most telling moment

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.940
comes when Entertainment asked how
he felt about the ending:

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.259
"There are no better writers in television
than Dan Weiss and David Benioff...You people

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.680
are in for it."

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.560
Some fans described the interview as a, quote,
"hostage video."

